19. independent reviewer reproduction and timeout correction

The independent reproduction supplied after the initial implementation did not
pass and remains part of the evidence:

- `corepack pnpm run test:editorial:e2e`: exit 1; 2 passed and 2 failed in
  3.3 minutes. Both failures exhausted the former 5-second locator wait for
  `[data-map-status='ready']`.
- `corepack pnpm run test:e2e`: exit 1 under four-worker contention. Failures
  included delayed MapLibre canvas/readiness, axe browser-context startup, and
  keyboard focus; all exhausted the former 30-second test budget.
- `corepack pnpm run ci`: exit 1 in the complete unit stage; 22 files passed,
  one file failed, 166 tests passed and 9 were skipped. The
  `headless-acceptance.test.ts` `beforeAll` exhausted its former 60-second
  budget after 139.91 seconds of process time.

The Playwright traces contained no application console exception. In the
failed editorial trace, Vite did not report connected until roughly 20.6
seconds after navigation and React initialization followed roughly two seconds
later. The error context subsequently captured the map in its ready state.
Together with the slow transform/import timings in the independent log, this
isolated wall-clock resource contention rather than a failed product assertion.

Correction, without retries, skipped cases, reduced sample counts, or weakened
assertions:

- Playwright is serialized to one worker, with a 180-second test/server budget
  and 60-second assertion budget.
- Each deterministic headless artifact construction receives 240 seconds. The
  fixed seed, 50 samples per difficulty, replay hashes, expected observables,
  and all nine acceptance assertions are unchanged.

Corrective verification:

- Concurrent stress run of `corepack pnpm run test:headless` and
  `corepack pnpm run test:editorial:e2e`: both exit 0; headless 9/9 in 302.59
  seconds total and editorial browser 4/4 in 2.4 minutes.
- `corepack pnpm run test:e2e`: exit 0; 24/24 in 6.3 minutes with one worker.
- `corepack pnpm run ci`: exit 0. Formatting, peer checks, lint and typecheck
  passed; complete unit suite passed 23 files / 175 tests in 336.59 seconds;
  deterministic bytes, byte-identical fixture builds, forbidden import and
  randomness negatives, editorial conformance, and governance/toolchain schema
  checks all passed.
- `py -3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests/governance -p "test_*.py" -v`:
  the sandboxed WindowsApps launcher was denied, and the exact escalated retry
  exited 0 with 7/7 tests passing in 0.279 seconds.

This correction improves test reliability only. It does not convert any human
review row or production gate to PASS, and Prompt 24 remains READY_FOR_REVIEW.
